{
  "tema": 10027,
  "slug": "tardarse-demorarse",
  "titulo": "Using tardar(se) / demorar(se) = to take time",
  "subtitulo": "Me tardo diez minutos en llegar: the person is the subject.",
  "foto": "t08.jpg",
  "regla": "Tardar(se) / demorar(se) + time + en + infinitive: the person (or the vehicle) is the subject. Never me tarda or te tardó.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say how long it takes someone to do something, Spanish uses **tardar** or **demorar**, often with a pronoun: **tardarse**, **demorarse**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "person + **tardar(se)**",
            "time",
            "**en**",
            "infinitive"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The big difference with English: the **person** is the subject, not _it_. **Yo tardo cinco minutos** = _it takes me five minutes_. So the verb agrees with the person."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "English",
            "Spanish"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "It takes me 5 minutes.",
              "Tardo / Me tardo / Me demoro 5 minutos."
            ],
            [
              "How long did it take you?",
              "¿Cuánto (te) tardaste? / ¿Cuánto te demoraste?"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The pronoun versions (**me tardo**, **te demoraste**) are very common in Mexico."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "With transportation, the **bus, train or plane** is the subject: **el camión tarda una hora**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Never build it like **gustar**: **me tarda** or **te tardó** are wrong."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: you're the one who's slow, not _it_. The verb points at you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Tardo== cinco minutos en llegar al taller.",
              "en": "It takes me five minutes to get to the shop."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Me tardo== cinco minutos en llegar al taller.",
              "en": "It takes me five minutes to get to the shop."
            },
